---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab library load documents (`event.category`
  `library`) per window, host, and library file. Other documents pass through
  unchanged.

  The first load of every library file in a window passes through
  immediately and unchanged, with the loading process. Further loads of the
  file in the same window are repeats: when the window closes, one summary
  document stands for them, and a file without repeats gets no summary. A
  summary stays an ECS library document. `event.start` and `event.end` hold
  the times of the first and last repeat, `event.duration` the time between
  them in nanoseconds, and `@timestamp` equals `event.start`. ECS has no
  field for the number of events that a document stands for, so
  `tenzir.count` holds the number of repeats, which excludes the first load,
  and `tenzir.distinct_pids` the number of distinct loading process IDs. Only
  summaries have `tenzir.count`.

  The key covers the library's path, hashes, and code signature and its
  `file.size`, so another binary at the same path gets its own summary.
  HarfangLab identifies the loading process mostly by its process ID alone.
  A summary keeps the process ID and executable of the loading process only
  if all repeats came from the same one.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1d
      description: Width of the deduplication windows, in processing and event
        time.
---

if event.category?.first() == "library" {
  _host = host?.id? else agent?.id? else host?.hostname?
  _time = time(this["@timestamp"]?)
  _bucket = _time.floor($window)
  window size=$window {
    // A digest of the keys keeps the state of the first-occurrence check
    // small. The summary below groups by the same keys.
    _key = hash_md5([_host, _bucket, dll?.path?, dll?.hash?.sha256?,
      dll?.hash?.sha1?, dll?.hash?.md5?, dll?.code_signature?.valid?,
      dll?.code_signature?.subject_name?, file?.size?])
    summarize _key, _seen=count(), options={mode: "cumulative"}
    if _seen == 1 {
      drop _key, _host, _time, _bucket, _seen
    } else {
      // All keys are scalars. The records come from the first repeat: the
      // host, agent, and organization belong to the host, the library record
      // to the keyed path, hashes, and code signature.
      summarize _host, _bucket, event?.kind?, event?.type?, dll?.path?,
        dll?.hash?.sha256?, dll?.hash?.sha1?, dll?.hash?.md5?,
        dll?.code_signature?.valid?, dll?.code_signature?.subject_name?,
        file?.size?,
        count=count(), start=min(_time), end=max(_time),
        _host_record=first(host?), _agent=first(agent?),
        _organization=first(organization?), _ecs=first(ecs?),
        _dll=first(dll?),
        _pids=count_distinct(process?.pid?), _pid=min(process?.pid?),
        _pid_count=count(process?.pid?),
        _executables=distinct(process?.executable?),
        _executable_count=count(process?.executable?)
      _pid = _pid if _pids == 1 and _pid_count == count else null
      _executable = (_executables[0]
        if _executables.length() == 1 and _executable_count == count
        else null)
      this = {
        "@timestamp": start,
        agent: _agent,
        dll: _dll,
        ecs: _ecs,
        event: {
          category: ["library"],
          kind: event.kind,
          type: event.type,
          start: start,
          end: end,
          duration: int((end - start) / 1ns),
        },
        file: file,
        host: _host_record,
        organization: _organization,
        process: {executable: _executable, pid: _pid},
        tenzir: {count: count, distinct_pids: _pids},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
